Package: lnav
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: openssh-client
Suggests: wl-clipboard | xclip
Description: log file navigator for the terminal
 lnav merges log files from many sources into a single view ordered by
 timestamp. It recognises common formats (syslog, journald, Apache and nginx
 access logs, JSON lines and more) on its own, highlights errors and
 warnings, follows files as they grow, opens compressed files and archives,
 and lets you query the log messages with SQL. It can also open logs on a
 remote host over ssh (lnav user@host:/var/log/syslog).
 .
 This package ships upstream's statically linked build, so it has no runtime
 dependencies, plus the man page. Debug info is stripped; the symbol table is
 kept for crash backtraces. openssh-client is recommended for remote logs,
 and wl-clipboard or xclip lets lnav copy to the system clipboard.
